{%- comment -%}
  The stable identity of the AGENT a token belongs to — the one definition.

  A person's choices about an assistant (which tools it may use) are stored
  against this key, and the call path checks against it. If the key were derived
  in two places they could drift, and a switched-off tool would silently work
  again, so both the panel and `identity/resolve_principal` call this.

  The OAuth `client_id` when the token has one: it survives a refresh, where the
  token row's digests rotate and a per-token choice would be lost. Otherwise the
  human label, so two manual keys a person labelled the same way are one
  assistant. Otherwise the principal itself, for an unlabelled manual token.

  @param {object} token - an mcp_token row (needs client_id, label, user_id)
  @return {string} the agent key, never blank for a token bound to a user
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  assign fallback = 'user:' | append: token.user_id
  assign key = token.label | default: fallback
  assign key = token.client_id | default: key
  return key
%}
